\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
Sable derivative ledger. The independently declared cursor entity is $g$. The polynomial map is reviewed on the stated variable and the public condition is asserted. Public law first-derivative-relation roles, in compiled order: derivative, function, variable. The reviewed condition is asserted: function-differentiable [differentiable] subjects function, variable. The function is differentiable with respect to the stated variable. \[g'(s)=3s^2\]
\end{document}

\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
Juniper graph census. The independently declared cursor entity is $m$. The finite undirected graph census binds both quantities to one graph. Public law handshaking-degree-sum roles, in compiled order: degree-sum, edge-count. The reviewed condition is asserted: declared-domain [domain-membership] subjects degree-sum, edge-count. Every role is explicitly bound to its declared semantic domain. \[\Sigma_d=2m\]
\end{document}

\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
Willow duct traverse. The independently declared cursor entity is $Q$. The traverse reports the area-mean normal component for one cross-section. Public law volumetric-flow-rate roles, in compiled order: flow-rate, area, velocity. The reviewed condition is asserted: mean-normal-velocity [assumption] subjects area, velocity. Velocity is the area-mean component normal to the stated cross-section. \[Q_s=A_sv_s\]
\end{document}

\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
Amber calorimeter draft. The independently declared cursor entity is $H$. The draft states mass and specific heat but leaves the temperature change out of the relation. Public law sensible-heat-relation roles, in compiled order: heat-transfer, mass, specific-heat, temperature-change. The candidate condition is catalogued but is not established by this draft: constant-specific-heat [uniform] subjects specific-heat, temperature-change. Specific heat is treated as constant over the stated temperature interval and no phase change occurs. \[H_r=m_rc_r\]
\end{document}

\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
Cedar reactor margin. The independently declared cursor entity is $u$. Differentiability is asserted, while the equality and source side remain unwritten. Public law linear-first-order-ode roles, in compiled order: state, variable, coefficient, source. The candidate condition is catalogued but is not established by this draft: state-differentiable [differentiable] subjects state, variable. The state is differentiable with respect to the evolution variable. \[u'(t)+a(t)u(t)\]
\end{document}

\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
Moss operand notebook. The operands are left untyped, so the note does not select the set universe or probability-space reading. Public law set-union roles, in compiled order: left, right. The candidate condition is catalogued but is not established by this draft: common-set-domain [domain-membership] subjects left, right. Both operands are sets in the active universe. The candidate condition is catalogued but is not established by this draft: common-probability-space [same-context] subjects left, right. Both operands are events in a common probability space. \[A\cup B\]
\end{document}

\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
Beryl standpipe comparison. The independently declared cursor entity is $p$. The focus notation is independently declared, but the line never chooses whether height is depth-positive or elevation-positive. Public law hydrostatic-pressure roles, in compiled order: pressure, density, acceleration, height. The candidate condition is catalogued but is not established by this draft: hydrostatic-regime [assumption] subjects pressure, density, acceleration, height. The fluid is at rest, density is constant, and the stated vertical sign convention is used. \[p_\diamond=\rho gh\]
\end{document}

\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
Ochre thermal network margin. The letter used on the right is also introduced as a gas constant in the surrounding margin, and no scope selects a meaning. Public law thermal-resistance-rate roles, in compiled order: temperature-change, heat-transfer-rate, resistance. The candidate condition is catalogued but is not established by this draft: declared-domain [domain-membership] subjects temperature-change, heat-transfer-rate, resistance. Every role is explicitly bound to its declared semantic domain. \[\Delta T_\triangle=\dot Q_\triangle R_\triangle\]
\end{document}

\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
Crimson initial-data collision. Both displayed values are asserted for the same state and initial time in one initial-value problem. Public law initial-value-condition roles, in compiled order: state, initial-time, initial-value. The reviewed condition applies to both competing assertions: same-context [same-context] subjects state, initial-time, initial-value. The state, time, and value belong to the same initial-value problem. \[y(0)=1\]
\[y(0)=2\]
\end{document}

\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
Umber cardinality dispute. The same two finite sets are asserted to obey both the subtraction and addition versions. Public law two-set-inclusion-exclusion roles, in compiled order: union-cardinality, left-cardinality, right-cardinality, intersection-cardinality. The reviewed condition applies to both competing assertions: declared-domain [domain-membership] subjects union-cardinality, left-cardinality, right-cardinality, intersection-cardinality. Every role is explicitly bound to its declared semantic domain. \[|D\cup C|=|D|+|C|-|D\cap C|\]
\[|D\cup C|=|D|+|C|+|D\cap C|\]
\end{document}

\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
Pine impeller heuristic. The independently declared cursor entity is $\rho$. The focus notation is independently declared, but the cubic-velocity heuristic is not the public dimensionless definition. Public law reynolds-number-definition roles, in compiled order: reynolds-number, density, velocity, length, viscosity. The candidate condition is catalogued but is not established by this draft: declared-domain [domain-membership] subjects reynolds-number, density, velocity, length, viscosity. Every role is explicitly bound to its declared semantic domain. \[\mathrm{Re}_x=\rho v^3\ell/\mu\]
\end{document}

