Gold foil thermal guess. The squared-temperature guess supplies neither a gradient nor an isotropic conduction declaration. Public law fourier-conduction roles, in compiled order: flux, conductivity, temperature. The candidate condition is catalogued but is not established by this draft: isotropic-conduction [domain-membership] subjects flux, conductivity, temperature. Flux, conductivity, and temperature are explicitly bound in the stated conduction model. \[q''_\dagger=kT^2\]
\end{document}
